+# `x86_64-unknown-muffin`
+
+**Tier: 3**
+
+Userspace of [muffin](https://github.com/muffin-os/muffin), a hobby operating
+system for x86_64.
+
+## Target maintainers
+
+[@tsatke](https://github.com/tsatke)
+
+## Requirements
+
+This target is cross-compiled. There are no special requirements for the host.
+
+Binaries are static `ET_EXEC` ELF files. The muffin loader does not accept
+position-independent executables. Code uses SSE2 for floats and leaves AVX off,
+because the kernel saves the FPU state with `fxsave`. Panics unwind.
+
+std runs on the unix platform layer. The `libc` crate and the C runtime
+`muffinos-rt` from the muffin repository supply the C symbols that std calls.
+
+## Building the target toolchain
+
+The muffin repository builds the sysroot crates with Bazel and does not use
+`x.py` for them. It builds only this compiler with `x.py`:
+
+```sh
+./x.py build --stage 2 compiler
+```
+
+`support/rust/bootstrap.toml.tpl` in the muffin repository holds the
+`bootstrap.toml` of that build.
+
+## Building Rust programs
+
+Rust does not ship pre-compiled artifacts for this target. Build `core`,
+`alloc` and `std` from the muffin repository with `bazel build //support/rust`.
+
+## Testing
+
+The muffin repository runs its binaries in QEMU through `bazel test //tests/...`.
+The Rust test suite does not run on this target.
+
+## Cross-compilation toolchains and C code
+
+C code is not supported.
